<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="013" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>B-1 decision capability: list and plan</title>
    <phase>A BFF rework</phase>
    <gate>after 017</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags include bff-api; creates a service and modifies endpoints (.cs)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>New abstraction: the transport-free decision capability shared by REST and MCP, extracted on Services/Signals/** owned by ontology-platform</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>B</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Shares no file with 002 (owner-run steps and notes only); serial with 014 and 016 through deps</parallel-reason>
    <deps>011, 017</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, api, refactoring, di, unit-test, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Create the self-authorising decision capability (IDecisionCapability) with the Decide-lane list and the decision plan operations. Its methods take the caller from the request: the HttpContext, or the ClaimsPrincipal where that is enough. Make the worklist, decision-plan and suppression REST endpoints thin adapters over it, with their responses unchanged.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in layered ASP.NET Core service design and behaviour-preserving extraction.</role>
  <goal>IDecisionCapability and DecisionCapability exist in Services/Signals/ with ListDecideAsync and GetPlanAsync (plan + suppression + full row, writes the plan-read stamp); the REST endpoints call them; 011's baselines pass unchanged.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Design §7 and §8 B-1; spec FR-10, FR-06. Read rules in SignalReadService (core-record check; 503 too_many_signals instead of a partial list) are unchanged. Category filtering is presentation and lives in 022, not here. The capability layer is IDecisionCapability (list, plan, commit) plus IDecisionLookupSearch (016). Caller context (FR-10 as amended 2026-11-07, owner option C; ICallerContext deferred): B-1 only moves the endpoint bodies into capability methods. ListDecideAsync takes the ClaimsPrincipal and calls SignalReadService.ReadAsync(set, user, ct). GetPlanAsync and GetSuppressionAsync take the HttpContext and run the DecisionPlanEndpoints body unchanged: SignalCoreRecordAccess, DecisionPlanService.GetAsync, DecisionPlanReadStamp.StampAsync(http) and DecisionParameterSources.OptionsAsync(http). REST passes the endpoint's HttpContext; MCP tools (022, 023) pass IHttpContextAccessor.HttpContext.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/IDecisionCapability.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/DecisionCapability.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Signals/SignalReadEndpoints.cs (GetWorklistAsync → capability)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Signals/DecisionPlanEndpoints.cs (GetDecisionPlanAsync, GetSuppressionAsync → capability)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/SignalsModule.cs (AddScoped IDecisionCapability)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/domain/Signals/DecisionCapabilityListPlanTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/auth/Signals/DecisionCapabilityCallerTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/SignalReadService.cs (worklist pipeline, L308; too_many_signals L661)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/DecisionPlanReadStamp.cs (stamp key and 4 h TTL)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/SignalsModule.cs (module registration style)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="011" status="pending">Golden baselines</dependency>
      <dependency task="017" status="pending">DecisionResultMapper used by the thin endpoints</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">The REST responses of GET /api/v1/signals/worklist, GET /api/v1/signals/{id}/decision-plan, GET /api/v1/signals/{id}/suppression and POST /api/v1/signals/{id}/decision stay byte-for-byte unchanged: task 011's contract baseline tests pass with no golden-file edit (FR-09).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Every operation this task adds or changes takes the caller from the request. Capability methods receive the HttpContext the REST endpoint already has (or its ClaimsPrincipal where that is enough) and pass it to the existing decision services unchanged. A null HttpContext or an unauthenticated caller returns DataverseUserClientErrorCodes.UserContextRequired (DATAVERSE_USER_CONTEXT_REQUIRED), and nothing falls back to an app-only client (FR-10 as amended 2026-11-07, option C; ADR-002 WP-6 fail closed). No ICallerContext or other caller holder is introduced.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">In every file this task touches, SignalReadService read rules and DecisionCommitService validation, idempotency and execution order are unchanged; DecisionCommitService stays the single owner of completion; SignalWriter, DecisionRecordWriter and DecisionCallerRights are not edited.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">IDecisionCapability signatures take the request HttpContext, or a ClaimsPrincipal where that is enough (ListDecideAsync). They contain no HttpRequest, IResult or MCP SDK type, and results are the existing domain result types (SignalReadResult etc.).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">GetPlanAsync writes the plan-read stamp exactly as the plan route does today (same key, 4 h TTL, same conditions), and writes none when the plan is refused.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">The capability is registered as Scoped in SignalsModule.cs; no new module.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">File ownership for parallel safety: this task creates IDecisionCapability.cs and DecisionCapability.cs; 014 adds the commit members; 015 adds the page member; 016 does not edit them.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Every PR from this task that touches Services/Signals/**, Api/Signals/** or the worklist route is reviewed by spaarke-ontology-platform-r1 before merge (project CLAUDE.md §4); run /conflict-check before opening it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">Every change this task makes under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ is listed in the PR with a Placement Justification that cites .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (source text: spec.md 'Placement Justification'), and the PR records the publish-size delta against a fresh master build per .claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md 'BFF Publish-Size Per-Task Verification Rule': a delta of +5 MB or more needs explicit justification, a total of 55 MB or more triggers architecture review, and the total must stay at or under 60 MB (hard stop). No new HIGH CVE (dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Every test this task adds lives on a KEEP path (tests/integration/{auth,contract,regression,data-mutation}/** or tests/unit/domain/**), mocks only at module boundaries, and uses no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; or Mock&lt;IServiceClient&gt;.</constraint>
  </constraints>

