  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read SignalReadEndpoints.GetWorklistAsync, DecisionPlanEndpoints.GetDecisionPlanAsync/GetSuppressionAsync and the services they call.</step>
    <step order="2">Create IDecisionCapability (ListDecideAsync(ClaimsPrincipal user, ct), GetPlanAsync(HttpContext http, signalId, ct), GetSuppressionAsync(HttpContext http, signalId, ct)) and DecisionCapability. Move the endpoint bodies into it unchanged, including their calls that take the HttpContext; leave only HTTP result shaping in the endpoints.</step>
    <step order="3">Reduce the three endpoints to: call capability → DecisionResultMapper.ToHttp.</step>
    <step order="4">Register the capability in SignalsModule.cs.</step>
    <step order="5">Write the tests in the acceptance criteria; run 011's baselines and the Signals suites (including the one-batched-BillingEventRead count).</step>
    <step order="6">Measure the publish-size delta; open the PR for ontology review stating that read rules are unchanged.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="8">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If extracting the plan logic would change when or how the plan-read stamp is written, STOP and escalate.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any 011 baseline changes, STOP (AP-9).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>SignalReadService.cs, DecisionPlanReadStamp.cs and the plan/worklist endpoint bodies (DecisionPlanEndpoints.cs, SignalReadEndpoints.cs) hold this logic today.</existing>
    <extension>Yes, it extends them: the endpoint bodies move into one entry point whose methods take the request HttpContext or ClaimsPrincipal; no new rules.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>MCP tools would have to call endpoint code or re-derive the caller and plan logic, giving the plan-read stamp and read rules a second owner (spec §11 table).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test .NET projects (dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/, dotnet test)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/IDecisionCapability.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/DecisionCapability.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/domain/Signals/DecisionCapabilityListPlanTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/auth/Signals/DecisionCapabilityCallerTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">IDecisionCapability exposes ListDecideAsync(ClaimsPrincipal, ct), GetPlanAsync(HttpContext, Guid, ct) and GetSuppressionAsync(HttpContext, Guid, ct), with no HttpRequest, IResult or MCP SDK type in any signature.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The worklist, decision-plan and suppression endpoints call the capability; 011's baselines pass with no golden change.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">GetPlanAsync writes the plan-read stamp with the same key and TTL as before (test asserts presence after a plan read).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: for a Signal outside the caller's core-record access, GetPlanAsync returns the same reason code the REST route returns and writes no stamp.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: with a null HttpContext or an unauthenticated principal, the list and plan operations return UserContextRequired and make no Dataverse call.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The 503 too_many_signals path and the one-batched-BillingEventRead count are unchanged (existing tests pass).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The PR records the publish-size delta (at or under 60 MB, no new HIGH CVE) and the ontology review.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Design §7 names the list operation DecisionCapability.ListDecideAsync. Keep the list unfiltered; category partitioning is 022's (parity with laneCountFilters.ts).

Completion (2026-11-07, commits 51f124bb6d + review fix ffe5b3a84f):
- DecisionCapability (Services/Signals, sealed partial) + IDecisionCapability: ListDecideAsync(ClaimsPrincipal?, ct, set = Lanes), GetPlanAsync(HttpContext?, Guid, ct), GetSuppressionAsync(HttpContext?, Guid, ct); no HttpRequest, IResult or MCP SDK type in a signature. The worklist, plan and suppression endpoints are thin adapters through DecisionResultMapper (new typed overloads for DecisionPlanReadResult / SuppressionReadResult). Registered scoped in SignalsModule. Caller guard: no context or no authenticated identity is UserContextRequired (401, same reasonCode on the tool error) before any Dataverse call. Deviations and decisions: notes/decisions.md "2026-11-07 — Task 013".
- Escalation triggers: neither fired. The plan-read stamp call, arguments and position are unchanged (last, only on a returned plan); 011 baselines 63/63 (53 plan/suppression/decision + 10 worklist), no golden file edited.
- Tests: new DecisionCapabilityCallerTests (tests/integration/auth/Signals), DecisionCapabilityListPlanTests + DecisionCapabilityFixtures (tests/unit/domain/Signals), mapper parity rows. Fail-before: guard removed fails 9/10 caller tests; stamp moved above the inquiry check fails 4 DoLanePrivacy cases; reason-based no-caller match fails the new mapper test. Signals domain/auth/contract filter 2939/2939; SignalReadRouteTests (integration, incl. 10 worklist baselines, 503 too_many_signals, batched count) 128/128; ArchTests 1973/1973 (RouteAuthorizationGuard 93/93 after the ledger fix); full unit suite: stopped after about 80 min on a machine shared with another session's test run; 40 failures, all outside Signals (Compose, Office, Documents, Insights, ExternalAccess, an eval harness), each after 1.5 to 18 min, i.e. host timeouts under contention. A sample of 23 of those re-run alone passed 23/23.
- Build: Sprk.Bff.Api 0 warnings, 0 errors (TreatWarningsAsErrors).
- Publish size (dotnet publish -c Release, framework-dependent linux-x64, Compress-Archive Optimal over deploy/api-publish/*, PDBs included, fresh short-path worktrees C:\wt013m / C:\wt013b, 191 files each side): master d53d67f604 = 39.26 MB (41,162,509 B); branch 51f124bb6d = 39.24 MB (41,147,135 B); branch vs master -15,374 B. Task delta vs 017's measured 21882337f7 (41,143,201 B): about +3.9 KB. Under 55/60 MB. dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive: no vulnerable packages.
- Quality gates: adversarial review (opus), one pass: no production defect; F3 x2 fixed (stamp-not-written on the 503 inquiry paths now pinned; stale ledger line citation), K2 fixed (no-caller worklist matched by reference). Known limits: K1, the guard and stamp read the passed HttpContext while Dataverse reads use IHttpContextAccessor; same object on REST; 020/022 must pass the ambient context over a stateless host (FR-01). K3, the plan/suppression baseline host registers the capability by hand (the worklist host uses the real Program DI). K4, no golden for suppression.200 / partition-undetermined (pre-existing from 011; arms identical by inspection); result records have public constructors. Self review K4: per-request construction of the scoped capability (note for 014); ?? throw in the Ok factories. adr-check: ADR-001/002 WP-6/008/009/013/019/028/029/038/052 compliant; ADR-010 warning: IDecisionCapability has one implementation, kept per the POML and design §8 B-1 as the seam two hosts consume and 022-024 tool tests substitute (path C reasoning, no violation).
- Not done here: "full Work Item row" (goal text) left to 023 with 015's projection (decisions.md). The PR for ontology review is the main session's (brief: push only); the ontology review is noted in both commit bodies. Master sync: origin/master 23567b2f93 touches DecisionActionCatalogTests, DoLanePrivacyTests, SignalSuppressionTests; a trial merge-tree is clean.
rework: fix-round-1 task 013</notes>

